{"id": "MX-C-0003", "tier": "C", "stream": "Mathesis", "statement": "Survey of sibling Lean trees on 2026-08-13, by comment-stripped lexical scan (Tier C: lexical, not kernel -- those trees cannot be compiled from here). MechanicaFluidorum/lean_src: 0 axioms, 0 sorry. RajMathRecovery/dualscale/lean/DualScale: 34 axiom declarations across 14 files, plus 2 sorry in Physics/HolographicDemonstration.lean. That stream's README states Rule R1 (no axiom declarations) and Rule R2 (sorry tracked as debt) are enforced by a CI file dualscale_ci.yml; no such file exists and the repository has no .github directory. The commit that introduced both sorry occurrences (e3a82fb) is titled 'zero-sorry Lean 4 verification'. Cross-stream contamination is LATENT, NOT LIVE: MechanicaFluidorum imports only Mathlib modules and uses the RajMathRecovery tree solely as a Mathlib provider via lake env, so no DualScale axiom currently enters any MechanicaFluidorum footprint; a single import line would change that, and MechanicaFluidorum's own footprint gate is what would catch it. Three overlaps are load-bearing if that import is ever written: aubin_lions_compactness is an axiom there (twice) and a hypothesis parameter in Stream 1; dyadic_cascade_conservation is an axiom there and a proved Tier A telescoping identity in Stream 1; enstrophy is axiomatized there and defined in Stream 1. Separately, the Reff duplicate that SPEC-STREAM0 section 1 expects does not exist: exactly one definition of Reff was found in all of xdev, and Stream 5's nearest analogue TDuality.lean instead fixes alpha_prime := 1 as a global constant and axiomatizes t_duality_invariance.", "evidence_kind": "argument", "artifact": "docs/designs/RECONCILIATION.md#4 + tests/tier_b_axiom_hygiene.py --survey", "supports": [], "audited_by": null, "supersedes": null}
{"id": "MX-A-0006", "tier": "A", "stream": "Mathesis", "statement": "UC1 (mathematics). The sum of the first n odd numbers equals n^2, for all natural n. Mathlib-free; footprint [propext, Quot.sound] inherited from omega's decision procedure, measured not assumed.", "evidence_kind": "lean_axioms", "artifact": "lean/Mathesis/Applications/OddSums.lean#sumOdd_eq_sq", "supports": [], "audited_by": null, "supersedes": null}
{"id": "MX-A-0007", "tier": "A", "stream": "Mathesis", "statement": "UC2 (physics). The standard 1-D elastic collision formulae conserve both momentum and kinetic energy exactly over the rationals, for any masses with m1 + m2 nonzero. The nonzero hypothesis is load-bearing: a witness exhibits momentum failing when m2 = -m1.", "evidence_kind": "lean_axioms", "artifact": "lean/Mathesis/Applications/ElasticCollision.lean#momentum_conserved,kinetic_energy_conserved", "supports": [], "audited_by": null, "supersedes": null}
{"id": "MX-A-0008", "tier": "A", "stream": "Mathesis", "statement": "UC3 (biology). Under the Hardy-Weinberg model, genotype frequencies sum to one, allele frequency is invariant under random mating, and equilibrium is reached in one generation from arbitrary starting genotype frequencies. This is a theorem about the MODEL; no claim is made about any population.", "evidence_kind": "lean_axioms", "artifact": "lean/Mathesis/Applications/HardyWeinberg.lean#genotype_freqs_sum_one,allele_freq_invariant,equilibrium_in_one_generation", "supports": [], "audited_by": null, "supersedes": null}
{"id": "MX-A-0009", "tier": "A", "stream": "Mathesis", "statement": "UC4 (physics). For circular orbits under an inverse-square central force, omega^2 * r^3 equals the gravitational parameter, and is therefore equal across any two orbits about the same primary. This is Kepler's third law with the reduced period tau = T/2pi, which removes pi from the statement and makes it exactly rational. The force law is a hypothesis parameter, never an axiom; the theorem is conditional on it.", "evidence_kind": "lean_axioms", "artifact": "lean/Mathesis/Applications/Kepler.lean#omega_sq_r_cubed,kepler_third", "supports": [], "audited_by": null, "supersedes": null}
{"id": "MX-A-0010", "tier": "A", "stream": "Mathesis", "statement": "UC5 (biology), algebraic core only. Substituting the Lotka-Volterra vector field into dV/dt and clearing the logarithmic derivatives yields a rational expression that is identically zero for nonzero populations. This is the algebraic content of the conservation law and requires no calculus. It does NOT establish that the expression is dV/dt; see MX-C-0004.", "evidence_kind": "lean_axioms", "artifact": "lean/Mathesis/Applications/LotkaVolterra.lean#dVdt_eq_zero", "supports": [], "audited_by": null, "supersedes": null}
